Docker [ Container Runtime Environment ] & [ " Doc + Worker " = Docker.] 

Docker is a containerization platform that allows you to: Package an application,Along with its dependencies, Into a lightweight unit called a container, And run it anywhere consistently. 
Interview Definition : Docker is an open-source containerization platform that packages applications and their dependencies into lightweight containers to ensure consistency across development, testing, and production environments.

Docker History 

Before Docker (Early Container Concepts)
Containers did NOT start with Docker.
1. 1979 – Unix Chroot
          Unix introduced: chroot
                           It allowed changing the root directory for a process.
                           This was the first step toward isolation.

2. 2000s – Linux Containers (LXC)
           Linux introduced: Namespaces and Cgroups
           These features allowed process isolation.
           Technology used: Linux Containers (LXC), But LXC was: Complex  and Not developer-friendly

3. Birth of Docker - 2013 – Docker Was Introduced
                     Docker was created by: Solomon Hykes
                     Under the company: Docker Inc.
                     Originally developed as part of: dotCloud
                     It has an bussiness of PAAS [ Platform as a Service ] 
                   
Why Docker Became Popular?

Docker made containers:Easy to use, Portable, Developer-friendly, CLI-based, Image-based system, It simplified LXC.

TimeLine of the Docker: 

